  "term": "radial nerve",
  "definition": "The radial nerve is a major nerve of the upper limb. It arises from lower neck and upper chest spinal cord fibers through the brachial plexus and provides movement to the arm’s extensor muscles as well as sensation to extensor areas of the arm and hand.",
